 "context": "<div data-type=\"note\" data-has-label=\"true\" id=\"fs-idp67599536\" class=\"interactive\" data-label=\"\">\n<h3 class=\"os-title\" data-type=\"title\">\n  <span class=\"os-title-label\">Link to Learning</span>\n</h3>\n<div class=\"os-note-body\">\n<h4 data-type=\"title\" id=\"8\" class=\"os-subtitle\">\n  <span class=\"os-subtitle-label\">Link to Learning</span>\n</h4>\n    <span data-type=\"media\" id=\"fs-idp124033248\" data-alt=\"QR Code representing a URL\">\n    <img src=\"https://openstax.org/apps/archive/20220509.174553/resources/0f6e0edeed17c9f817d2cf79b26face949665af6\" data-media-type=\"image/png\" alt=\"QR Code representing a URL\" width=\"120\" id=\"9\">\n    </span>\n    <p id=\"fs-idm38145824\">In 1915, biologist Ronald Fisher proposed another model of sexual selection: the <a href=\"https://openstaxcollege.org/l/sexual_select\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\">Fisherian runaway model</a>, which suggests that selection of certain traits is a result of sexual preference.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n",
